{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>The length of the one curtain.</b> The alef with pataḥ and the accent on the first — 'האחת' with alef in segol and the accent third — 'האחת,' its alef in segol, and likewise in the goat-hair curtains. In sum, all of them — their alef with pataḥ, and every etnaḥta, zaqef, and end of verse — their alef in segol."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The comment distinguishes two vocalizations of האחת: one with pataḥ (pausal), one with segol (contextual), and maps which accentual positions trigger which. 'תניינא' (Aramaic 'second') and 'תליתאה' ('third') refer to the accent's position within the word."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:33.655577030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}